.TH REV 1
.SH NAME
rev \- reverse the characters of each line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rev
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rev
copies each
.I file
(standard input if none given) to standard output with the characters of
every line reversed, last character first. Runes are reversed whole, not
their encoded bytes, so a line of Unicode text reverses correctly rather
than being scrambled.
.PP
The classic use is sorting on the end of a line instead of the start:
reversing, sorting, then reversing back groups lines by how they end.
.SH EXAMPLE
.TP
.EX
tr -cs A-Za-z '\en' <genesis | sort | uniq | rev | sort | rev
.EE
.IP
Unique words from
.B genesis,
grouped by the last few letters they share rather than the first.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/rev.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR sort (1),
.IR tac (1)
